  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\nAn upper level low will move eastward across the northern tier of\nMT tonight. This will allow for scattered showers and\nthunderstorms to continue over the CWA, with an area of steady\nrainfall continuing around Glacier Park and in the Cut Bank area.\nOn Tuesday, a 2nd upper level trof quickly moves eastward across\nthe southern half of the state, resulting in scattered\nshowers/thunderstorms over Southwest MT on Tue afternoon.\n\nBy Wednesday, the flow aloft becomes more zonal resulting in\nwarmer air slowly moving back into the CWA. The zonal flow will\nnot last long, as the next upper level low begins to approach the\nCWA by late on Friday. This upper level low moves over Central MT\nby Sunday. With cool temperatures, snow levels on Sunday will\nlower to around 7000 feet or so. Some snow accumulations are\nlooking likely, especially in Glacier Park. This system will begin\nto exit the CWA on Monday.\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\nThe continues to be a chance for flooding around Glacier Park, as\nperiods of rain continue into Tuesday.\n\nOtherwise, the main concern this weekend will be how low does the\nsnow level get. Currently we are thinking snow levels could be as\nlow as 7000 feet by Sunday morning. Current thinking is snow \naccumulations of 3 to 6 are possible at the highest elevations.",
